      "message": "Out of curiosity, is the return statement necessary? Do we run into potential problems if we skip the below decoder alarm check?\n\nAs understand it, it seems like as long as `MAX_A2DP_DELAYED_START_FRAME_COUNT` is less than `MAX_INPUT_A2DP_FRAME_QUEUE_SZ`, then we should have begun decoding before we can hit max size. I\u0027m not sure if it\u0027s possible, but I\u0027d worry if something happens like we leave the queue full after we stop decoding though. We might get into a cycle where we keep getting new packets and adding them to the already full queue, and never restart decoding.",
